--# Solution A — Asymmetric Cross-MAE: architecture diagrams
--
--PlantUML source for **Solution A (Modality-Isolated / Asymmetric Cross-MAE)**, the
--asymmetric variant of the current shared-encoder design (**Solution C**).
--
--Design of record: `code/notes/design/SolutionA_asymCrossMAE.md`.
--Both solutions share one dataset and one encoder interface; they differ **only** in the
--pre-training stage (see diagram 3).
--
-----
--
--#0 Solution A: Asymmetric Cross-MAE Architecture Workflow
--
--```plantuml
--@startuml
--skinparam componentStyle rectangle
--skinparam shadowing false
--skinparam packageStyle rectangle
--
--
--  
--    node "Inputs" {
--        [Thermal Video Stream] as TIR_Input
--        [Respiration Waveform] as RESP_Target
--    }
--
--    package "Visual Tokenization & Encoder" {
--        [Tubelet Patch Projection] as Projection
--        [Spatial-Temporal Tubelet Masking] as Masking
--        [ViT Encoder] as Encoder
--    }
--
--    package "TIR Reconstruction" {
--        [TIR Pixel Decoder (Self-Attention)] as TIR_Decoder
--        [TIR Pixel Loss] as Loss_TIR
--    }
--
--    package "RESP Reconstruction" {
--        [Learned Positional Queries] as Queries
--        [<font color=red>RESP Decoder (Cross-Attention)</font>] as RESP_Decoder
--        [RESP Waveform Loss] as Loss_RESP
--    }
--  
--
--    ' Stage 1 Data Flow
--    TIR_Input --> Projection
--    Projection --> Masking
--    Masking --> Encoder : Unmasked Visual Tokens Only
--  
--    Encoder --> TIR_Decoder : Latent Visual Embeddings
--    TIR_Decoder --> Loss_TIR
--    TIR_Input ..> Loss_TIR : Ground Truth Masked Pixels
--  
--    Encoder --> RESP_Decoder : Keys & Values
--    Queries --> RESP_Decoder : Queries
--    RESP_Decoder --> Loss_RESP
--    RESP_Target .[#red].> Loss_RESP : <font color=red>Ground Truth Alignment</font>
--
--
--@enduml
--```
--
--## 0.2 SL fine-tuning
--
--```plantuml
--
--@startuml
--
--package "Stage 2: Downstream Fine-Tuning (FT)" {
--  
--    [Full Unmasked Thermal Video] as FT_Input
--    [Pre-trained ViT Encoder] as FT_Encoder
--    [1D Temporal Regression Head] as Reg_Head
--    [Predicted Respiration Waveform] as Waveform_Output
--
--    ' Stage 2 Data Flow
--    FT_Input --> FT_Encoder
--    FT_Encoder --> Reg_Head
--    Reg_Head --> Waveform_Output
--}
--
--
--@enduml
--```
--
-----
--
--## 1. SSL pre-training — Solution A (resp tokens excluded from the encoder)
--
--```plantuml
--@startuml SolutionA_SSL
--skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
--skinparam shadowing false
--skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
--skinparam rectangle {
--  BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
--  BorderColor #4A6FA5
--}
--skinparam component {
--  BackgroundColor #E8F0FB
--  BorderColor #2E5A88
--}
--skinparam note {
--  BackgroundColor #FFF8DC
--  BorderColor #C8A951
--}
--
--title Solution A: Asymmetric Cross-MAE pre-training
--
--actor "BP4D raw tree\nThermal + IRFeatures + Resp_Volts" as RAW
--
--package "Dataset (identical for A and C)" as DS {
--  rectangle "Static clip ROI\n12 nose+mouth landmarks, +20% pad, one box per clip" as ROI
--  rectangle "Zero-variance guard\nraw spread < 0.01 V -> clip dropped" as GUARD
--  rectangle "Subject-disjoint split\nsplit_by = subject" as SPLIT
--}
--
--rectangle "x_TIR   [B,3,T,H,W]\nT=100, H=W=64" as XTIR
--rectangle "y_RESP   [B,L]\nL=800 raw volts, z-score per clip" as YRESP
--
--package "Encoder (SHARED by Solution A and Solution C)" as ENC {
--  component "TubeletEmbed\nConv3d 2x16x16 -> 800 visual tokens" as TOKVIS
--  component "Tube mask 90%\n-> 10% visible = 80 tokens" as MASKV
--  component "ViT Encoder\n12 blocks, D=768\nenc_blocks + enc_norm" as VIT
--}
--
--rectangle "Z_v   [B, 80, 768]\nvisual tokens ONLY, no resp tokens" as ZV
